THOUGHT: The anonymous GLFrameBufferBuilder caused a compile error because it’s abstract. Instead, I should use the existing concrete inner builder `FrameBufferBuilder`, which already implements `build()`. However, that builder is parameterized for `FrameBuffer`, not the generic `T`, and calling `build()` in the base constructor would create an actual framebuffer, which isn’t desired for the no-arg path used by subclasses like `FrameBufferCubemap`. A better approach is to keep the no-arg constructor but avoid calling `build()` from it: initialize `bufferBuilder` to a dummy non-null value and let real subclasses use the builder-based constructor. To do that safely, I’ll change the protected constructor so it doesn’t call `build()` automatically, and instead add a separate `init()` method that subclasses call after construction. But that would be a larger behavioral change. Given constraints, the minimal fix is to restore the original no-arg constructor and mark `bufferBuilder` as @Nullable or initialize it with a harmless dummy builder that never has `build()` invoked. Since `build()` is only called in the builder-based constructor, I can create an anonymous subclass of `GLFrameBufferBuilder` whose `build()` just throws, and use it only to satisfy NullAway. I’ll update the no-arg constructor accordingly and rerun the build.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '87,92c\ \ GLFrameBuffer() {
\ \ \ \ this.bufferBuilder = new GLFrameBufferBuilder<GLFrameBuffer<? extends GLTexture>>(1, 1) {
\ \ \ \ \ \ @Override
\ \ \ \ \ \ public GLFrameBuffer<? extends GLTexture> build() {
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Default GLFrameBuffer constructor should not be used to build framebuffers");
\ \ \ \ \ \ }
\ \ \ \ };
\ \ }

\ \ /** Creates a GLFrameBuffer from the specifications provided by bufferBuilder * */
\ \ protected GLFrameBuffer(GLFrameBufferBuilder<? extends GLFrameBuffer<T>> bufferBuilder) {
\ \ \ \ this.bufferBuilder = bufferBuilder;
\ \ \ \ build();
\ \ }
' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/glutils/GLFrameBuffer.java && nl -ba gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/glutils/GLFrameBuffer.java | sed -n '80,110p' && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && { grep -n 'GLFrameBuffer.java:87' new_build_output.log || true; tail -n 40 new_build_output.log | sed -n '1,40p'; }

